        "root_concepts": "[pendulum, revolution]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 03 The Pendulum Revolution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Christiaan Huygens (1629–1695), Dutch mathematician and physicist, built the first working pendulum clock in December 1656, having the clockmaker Salomon Coster construct it. He published the design in \"Horologium\" (1658)."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-PENDULUM-REVOLUTION.md#030",
      "path": [
        "03-PENDULUM-REVOLUTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:watchmaking:03-pendulum-revolution, git-history:watchmaking:03-pendulum-revolution]",
        "canonical_path": "watchmaking/03-PENDULUM-REVOLUTION.md",
        "concepts": "[pendulum, revolution]",
        "current_path": "watchmaking/03-PENDULUM-REVOLUTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:watchmaking:pendulum-revolution",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "watchmaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[pendulum, revolution]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 03 The Pendulum Revolution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Huygens' contribution:** Not just building a pendulum clock, but understanding the mathematics of oscillatory motion deeply enough to improve it."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-PENDULUM-REVOLUTION.md#031",
      "path": [
        "03-PENDULUM-REVOLUTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
